      "description": "Watch Atalanta vs Sassuolo highlights and goals from Serie A on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on August 23, 2026. The stage was set for a classic encounter as two determined sides faced off in a match where tactical discipline and individual errors would dictate the outcome. Both teams displayed high energy from the kickoff, signaling a contest that would be decided by the narrowest of margins. Atalanta Strike Early On August 23, 2026 , Atalanta asserted their dominance early in this Serie A fixture. It took only six minutes for the deadlock to be broken when Gianluca Gaetano provided a brilliant assist for Giacomo Raspadori . The forward made no mistake, firing a clinical left-footed shot into the net to give the home side a 1-0 lead. This early breakthrough allowed Atalanta to control the tempo for much of the first half, retaining 56% of the ball. Sassuolo struggled to find their rhythm in the opening 45 minutes. Despite several set-piece opportunities delivered by Armand Lauriente , the visitors could not test the goalkeeper effectively. Atalanta headed into the halftime break with a slender but well-deserved lead, looking comfortable in their defensive shape. A Seesaw Second Half The momentum shifted ten minutes into the second half. Following a defensive lapse by Odilon Kossounou , Sassuolo found a lifeline. Cas Odenthal rose highest to meet the ball from close range, powering a header into the net in the 55th minute to equalize. The goal breathed new life into the visitors, but their joy would be short-lived as Atalanta responded with a triple substitution to regain control. In the 65th minute, another defensive blunder, this time by Sassuolo’s Tommaso Macchioni , proved fatal. Substitute Nikola Krstovic seized the opportunity, striking the ball with his right foot. A lucky deflection took the ball past the goalkeeper and into the net, restoring Atalanta's lead and punishing the visitors' inconsistency at the back. Late Scares and Final Whistle The closing stages were frantic as Sassuolo pushed for a second equalizer. Simone Cinquegrano had a glorious chance in the 94th minute, but he failed to connect cleanly with a volley, sending the ball wide. At the other end, Giorgio Scalvini saw a header go agonizingly wide as Atalanta searched for a cushion. Ultimately, the brilliance of Marco Carnesecchi in goal ensured that Atalanta walked away with the 2-1 victory, surviving a late onslaught to secure all three points."
